WEBVTT

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:39.010
<b>Episode 7 
A Glorious Death</b>

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:41.880
An air raid siren...

00:01:42.650 --> 00:01:43.820
Quiet!

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.280
Everyone, prepare for takeoff.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.990
Line up on the runway.

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:48.790
Yes, sir!

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:59.390
At 1400, five enemy fighters entered 
the Mercurius flight zone.

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:02.610
After combat began, they fled toward Isla.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.060
We sustained minimal damage.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.770
The Aerial Knights gave chase immediately.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:11.420
Leave twenty Machina Deo to defend Isla.

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:14.070
All other planes are to launch 
with torpedoes and bombs.

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.570
Use all available planes.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.070
Even the trainees can at least do recon.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:20.910
Get the engines started!

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.200
Numbers 1 and 3 look good!

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:23.200
Get the pilots out here!

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.930
That air raid siren was not a drill...

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.460
You've been given the order to take off.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:32.840
The enemy is here. 
The knights are pursuing them.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.700
You will split into seven groups to search

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.970
a 120-degree area behind Isla.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.220
This mission is a very dangerous 
and important responsibility.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.850
Use what you've learned thus far 
to protect the skies of Isla.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:47.470
Roger.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.810
The following pilots will stay behind

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.980
to provide AA support over Centezual.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:55.040
Kal-el Albus.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.190
Claire Cruz.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.100
Ariel Albus.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.570
Ignacio Axis.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.730
Wolfgang Baumann.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:03.070
Marco Santos.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.790
All right, dismissed!

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:10.540
This will be our first mission...

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.500
Be careful!

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:15.530
But can we really handle an actual fight?

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:19.130
The knights will take out the enemy, 
so we won't have to do anything.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.510
We'll do our best without you, guys.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:22.910
Yeah...

00:03:22.910 --> 00:03:25.850
We've all trained for this day!

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.260
Come back safe, everyone.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.890
We'll see each other back here soon.

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:31.260
Yeah!

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.020
The guys sure are relaxed...

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.270
But will we really be all right?

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:45.240
What is that?

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:49.700
Main enemy force sighted at 1615.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.680
Looks like six destroyers providing support,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:56.250
two large, older wooden ships 
that seem to be battleships,

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.590
and one large, older wooden ship 
that appears to be a carrier.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:03.290
What a terrible fleet... It's totally beat-up.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:08.190
Enemy escorts sighted.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.100
All planes, attack!

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:18.050
Enemy escorts sighted.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:19.610
Beginning attack.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.130
Reporting... Enemy fleet sighted!

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:35.460
So they were there, after all.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.630
Divert all forces to the fight.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.710
Launch!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.310
Everyone's so lucky, getting to go on the recon...

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.610
Our mission is important, too.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:55.310
Yeah, I know.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.060
There's a car over there.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.030
They're waving at us.

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:05.140
Countess Ulshyrra?

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.730
Hmm? You know her?

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.490
Yeah.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.180
Claire Cruz and Ignacio Axis will stand by

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.210
in the central government office.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:19.630
The other students will stay here, 
awaiting further orders.

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:24.920
Now, come with me.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:30.220
I'm sorry, I have to go...

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:35.520
Wait!

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:37.170
Why does Claire...

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.940
Ignacio, too?

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.370
Why?

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:51.650
You are the governor of Isla.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:54.090
You're different than the pilots.

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:58.230
That's why I've appointed 
Ignacio as your bodyguard.

00:05:58.230 --> 00:06:00.650
You must keep that in mind at all times.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:04.710
But I've lost the power of the wind...

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.450
Given what's happening,

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:09.390
your duty is to inspire everyone from the center.

00:06:12.390 --> 00:06:14.390
As a figurehead, is it?

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:15.790
Did you say something?

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.300
Attacks are having no effect!

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.930
We'll open up a full barrage with our cannons.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.940
The enemy is currently withdrawing 
twenty degrees from Isla.

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.310
All forces are in pursuit.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.820
The <i>Luna Barco</i> is commencing 
direct bombardment.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:07.400
Don't you think it's strange

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:11.020
that they'd attack Isla with such a weak fleet?

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.210
It's possible this older fleet is 
a decoy, and their main fleet

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:19.790
is waiting in an ambush ahead, to surround 
and destroy the knight commander's forces.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:22.250
What's the surrounding area like?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.590
The students are carrying out recon right now.

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:28.810
Cloud cover, 7.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.870
240 nautical miles from the Escorial.

00:07:30.870 --> 00:07:32.550
All clear—

00:07:34.340 --> 00:07:38.090
Chiharu, bring us up. 
I saw something over there.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.040
Roger.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:40.980
I'll take us up to 3,500.

00:07:50.820 --> 00:07:52.950
No good, too many clouds...

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:54.980
Sure you didn't imagine it?

00:07:54.980 --> 00:07:57.420
Chiharu, bring us to the left.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:58.950
It's bothering me a bit.

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.850
Right.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:05.290
Mitty, over there!

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:14.270
Wh-What are those?

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:16.050
Large-scale bombers...

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:17.890
But they're huge!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:23.230
A-And a carrier!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.110
That's a carrier? 
I've never seen anything like that.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.740
It's filled with monoplane single-seat fighters.

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:32.280
And those are all escort fighters.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:35.600
That carrier's whole purpose 
is to escort the bombers?

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:36.520
Yes.

00:08:36.520 --> 00:08:40.790
They operate by an entirely different 
combat doctrine than we do.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.900
They sure don't look like barbarians to me.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:45.920
They look more advanced than we are.

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:55.380
We need to inform HQ.

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.970
1907...

00:08:57.230 --> 00:08:59.630
190 degrees, 240 nautical miles from Isla.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.830
We've sighted ultra-large enemy bombers.

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.850
Heading northeast, at 120 degrees.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.960
We will stay in range!

00:09:09.940 --> 00:09:12.000
We've wiped them out.

00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.490
Emergency transmission!

00:09:16.490 --> 00:09:18.090
Enemy bombers sighted!

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:20.150
Enemy formation includes an escort carrier!

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:21.500
Altitude 3,000...

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.910
Damn it! The fleet in front of us was a decoy!

00:09:24.360 --> 00:09:26.370
We were tricked by the barbarians?

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.070
Get all our planes there, now.

00:09:29.070 --> 00:09:31.290
And equip our escorts with bombs!

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:36.050
Mitsuo and Chiharu

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.510
have sighted enemies to the rear.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.130
They're still in enemy range.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.330
The enemy?

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.450
The ones in front wasn't their main force?

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:47.060
What should we do?

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.190
Stand by until we get orders.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:52.870
Wh-What do we do? It's impossible...

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:56.220
Mitsuo can't stay near them... 
He won't be able to do it!

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.240
They're both still trainees.

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.440
Can we ask HQ to recall them?

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.450
Have regular forces take their place?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:06.890
You can only use a single plane 
to stay in close recon.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.370
Bring multiple planes,

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:11.460
and the enemy is more likely 
to find and shoot you down.

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:15.070
The knights don't have any more planes.

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.170
I don't...

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:19.130
I never apologized to Mitsuo...

00:10:20.550 --> 00:10:22.940
I need him to come back.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:25.790
We should ask the teachers, right?

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:28.020
The teachers might be able to do something.

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:36.320
Where are you going?

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:38.060
Sonia.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.890
They're already back...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:44.650
That was fast.

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:46.120
Did they already beat them?

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:49.310
For a triumphant return, they're in a big rush.

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.170
Did something happen?

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.430
We won't learn anything if we stay here.

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:56.000
But I do want to know.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:00.300
It's our job to stay here, so we'll 
have to wait for orders!

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.660
No one will die, will they?

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:08.180
There's no such thing as a 
battle where no one dies.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:12.940
If there's a battle, even students 
will suffer casualties.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:15.210
This is a war.

00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.990
We have to be willing to risk our lives.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.400
Even if we lack skill,

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:23.120
we have the resolve.

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:26.080
But...

00:11:32.630 --> 00:11:35.570
Chiharu, cut the engines a little...

00:11:35.570 --> 00:11:36.970
They'll see the light.

00:11:37.990 --> 00:11:38.630
Yeah.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:45.790
No change in the enemy.

00:11:47.860 --> 00:11:49.890
Chiharu, get into cloud cover!

00:11:49.890 --> 00:11:51.440
Roger!

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.740
They're here...

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:11.700
Off our right side!

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:12.790
Look!

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:15.450
Red and blue navigation lights...

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.900
Those are Isla planes!

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:18.550
Yeah, those must be.

00:12:18.870 --> 00:12:20.180
I'm so glad...

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:21.540
They're here.

00:12:29.430 --> 00:12:30.650
Enemy sighted!

00:12:30.650 --> 00:12:33.220
The student report was right.

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:33.890
Yeah.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:43.330
What?

00:12:43.330 --> 00:12:45.070
The enemy navigation lights vanished!

00:12:45.400 --> 00:12:48.130
Now we can't attack!

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:50.910
All planes are already in attack formation.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:52.000
What should we do?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.030
If only we had the moon...

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.040
No way! They turned off their lights!

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.600
Won't they run into each other?

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.690
They must have real confidence in their skills.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:04.700
Otherwise, they'd never do this...

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:05.290
Yeah.

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:07.800
Our planes won't be able to attack now!

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.110
<i>If I fire this flare,</i>

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:16.890
<i>the enemy will see us for sure, and we'll die.</i>

00:13:16.890 --> 00:13:21.940
<i>But if I don't, our torpedo run is sure to fail.</i>

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.940
Hey, Mitty...

00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:30.830
You think everyone's worried 
about us right now?

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.570
I'm sure they're panicking.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:41.690
I can just hear Noripii going, 
"Will they be okay out there? No way."

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:43.840
Yeah, I bet.

00:13:44.710 --> 00:13:47.190
Nana's probably worried and panicking.

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:51.370
And Kal's saying, "It'll be fine," when he 
has no reason whatsoever to think so.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:53.190
And Ari's telling him to shut up.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:02.600
Mitty...

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:06.320
Let's fire the flare.

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:13.670
If we do, they'll shoot us down.

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:16.040
Yeah, I know.

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:19.960
But I don't want Isla to burn...

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:22.870
This would be much better.

00:14:24.610 --> 00:14:26.300
We trained so hard, right?

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:29.680
It'll be fine...

00:14:30.340 --> 00:14:32.140
Both of us will make it back.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.390
Got it. Let's do it!

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.410
<i>No matter what happens...</i>

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.800
<i>I'll make sure Chiharu gets back alive!</i>

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:49.590
A flare?

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:50.820
Was that the students?

00:15:06.280 --> 00:15:07.320
Head for their center!

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:10.210
We need to get higher, or we won't 
be able to light them all up!

00:15:10.210 --> 00:15:11.680
Yeah, I'll do my best!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:15.680
Thanks to you I can reach 
maximum altitude now!

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.830
Angle of inclination, 40 degrees, 5 to the right.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.560
Use twenty seconds emergency power!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:22.900
Right!

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.980
Just a bit more! Just a little more!

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:33.700
You can do it!

00:15:33.970 --> 00:15:36.080
We have to protect everyone...

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.540
We need to save Isla!

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:43.630
Right here!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:54.390
We did it.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:15:59.750
Where are the knights?

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:00.680
Over there!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:12.610
A textbook use of flares.

00:16:13.290 --> 00:16:17.400
Distance 25, 22, 20.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.740
Steady as she goes!

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.700
Fire!

00:16:28.910 --> 00:16:29.910
Hit!

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:40.410
They did it!

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:40.970
Yeah!

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:48.460
To our left!

00:16:48.460 --> 00:16:49.110
Slide!

00:16:49.430 --> 00:16:50.360
Roger!

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.690
Left! Left! Left!

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:54.610
Left!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:03.270
Left! Right! Right! Left!

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:15.590
I'm fine...

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:19.010
I can keep going!

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:21.210
We'll both go home together!

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:22.520
To Isla!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:29.900
Mitty?

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.760
Are you okay, Mitty?!

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:32.790
Mitty!

00:17:33.560 --> 00:17:34.990
I'm fine!

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:37.400
Keep your eyes forward, Chiharu!

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:37.910
Right.

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:41.810
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:43.570
<i>Father...</i>

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.890
<i>Mother...</i>

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:45.810
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:48.420
<i>But...</i>

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.670
<i>I'll save Chiharu, no matter what!</i>

00:17:51.490 --> 00:17:54.920
<i>I want to look good for the girl I love, at least!</i>

00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.680
Chiharu, eject.

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:02.330
Use your parachute and eject...

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:04.410
It'll be fine.

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.280
Our allies will pick you up midway.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:09.060
Then you jump, too.

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:12.130
Yeah, I'll jump, too.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:14.860
But you go first, Chiharu.

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.410
Really?

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:18.530
You'll jump with me?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:19.580
Yeah.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:20.600
Hurry.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:22.130
They'll shoot us down any minute...

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:23.000
Hurry!

00:18:24.540 --> 00:18:25.580
Okay.

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:42.430
Chiharu, promise me that you'll be a pilot.

00:18:54.890 --> 00:18:56.070
Mitty...

00:18:56.580 --> 00:18:58.400
Never give up!

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.200
Find the End of the Sky!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.580
Mitty!

00:19:15.120 --> 00:19:16.520
<i>This'll do...</i>

00:19:16.520 --> 00:19:18.460
<i>For me, I've done well.</i>

00:19:25.150 --> 00:19:26.110
Chiharu...

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.310
<i>I'm sorry, Mitty.</i>

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:57.670
<i>I'll be with you soon.</i>

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:10.150
Mr. Bandereas...

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:15.880
Ms. Sonia...

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:16.940
I'm sorry.

00:20:17.530 --> 00:20:19.140
We didn't make it in time.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:29.700
Mitty... Mitty! Mitty!

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:34.520
He was a true pilot.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.650
<i>Message from fortified cannon 
emplacement #2, Alondra.</i>

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.610
<i>We are under attack!</i>

00:21:04.140 --> 00:21:08.150
Until my father gets back, Isla is defenseless.

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:10.450
What should we do, Fausto?

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:13.060
What else?

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:19.920
El Halcons...

00:21:23.210 --> 00:21:24.130
Let's go, too.

00:21:24.390 --> 00:21:25.810
What are you talking about?

00:21:25.810 --> 00:21:27.470
Our orders are to stay here.

00:21:27.800 --> 00:21:29.890
But we need to defend Isla!

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:43.860
Fine... Get in.

00:21:46.690 --> 00:21:47.910
Ready to go!

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.250
Take off!

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:50.260
Take off!

00:23:31.800 --> 00:23:32.640
It's me, Ignacio.

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:36.640
That idiot ignored orders and took off.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:38.890
Is he trying to end up as fish food?

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:40.150
If I were—

00:23:39.950 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Episode 8: 
The Name of the Bird</b>
